            <ArticleTitle>Computed tomography guided lumbar sympathetic block for complex regional pain syndrome in a child: a case report and review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this paper is to describe the first reported use of computed tomography (CT) guided lumbar sympathetic block as treatment of a case of complex regional pain syndrome (CRPS) in a child. The potential aetiology of CRPS is discussed in relation to the mechanism of action of local anaesthetics used in the block. Based on the successful treatment of this child and the documented success of its use in adults, we conclude that despite the minimal dose of radiation given, CT guided lumbar sympathetic block is an important treatment option in CRPS in children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
